> @basvdlei Do you mind to try this PR with a fix in [this comment](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/95210#issuecomment-722994386) ? I haven't tested it yet, but I believe it should solve the problem you described.

@lingsamuel sorry for the late response. I made another build with your patch and as far as I can tell that works. At least for the metrics I use. Updating the timestamp on scrape should prevent the metrics from [becoming stale](https://www.robustperception.io/staleness-and-promql).

I was thinking about this though, and it does feel a little bit as a work-around. Since the timestamps have no meaning on the cached metrics, I'm wondering if there is some way we can drop them altogether.
